.TH "GLESHA-RUN" "1" "" "glesha" "User Commands"
.nh
.ad l
.SH NAME
glesha\-run \- create a snapshot and upload it
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBglesha run\fR SET [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Archive the sources of SET, encrypt the archive, and upload it to the set's remotes. The snapshot is full unless \-\-incremental is given.
.PP
An incremental snapshot stores the changes since the baseline snapshot and needs exactly one remote. Removed paths and type changes are confirmed first.
.PP
The local archive is deleted after a verified upload, unless \-\-output or \-\-keep\-archive is given. If no source changed, no snapshot is created.
.PP
If a run is interrupted, run it again or use 'glesha retry' to resume it. Options must match the interrupted run, and the same archive passphrase is required.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-full
Create a full snapshot (default).
.TP
.B \-\-incremental
Store only the changes since the baseline. Requires exactly one remote.
.TP
.B \-\-output FILE
Keep the archive at FILE, which must not exist.
.TP
.B \-\-assume\-yes
Answer yes to all confirmations. Confirms removed paths and type changes in an incremental snapshot.
.SS Remote options
.TP
.B \-\-to REMOTE...
Upload to REMOTE (default: the set's remotes).
.TP
.B \-\-from REMOTE...
Limit bucket access to REMOTE.
.PP
REMOTE... takes a comma\-separated list and may be repeated. If \-\-from or \-\-to is given, no other remote is accessed.
.SS Archive options
.TP
.B \-\-storage\-class CLASS
AWS storage class of this snapshot. Overrides the set's setting. Classes other than STANDARD require an AWS remote.
.TP
.B \-\-compression FORMAT
Compression: xz, gzip, or bzip2 (default: xz).
.TP
.B \-\-compression\-level N
Compression level, 1 to 9 (default: 6).
.TP
.B \-\-prefix PREFIX
Name prefix: glesha or encb (default: glesha).
.TP
.B \-\-archive\-mode MODE
Buffering: auto, memory, or stream (default: auto). With memory, the encrypted archive is held in memory and the command fails if it does not fit. With stream, it is written to a temporary file. With auto, it starts in memory and moves to a file when needed.
.TP
.B \-\-chunked
Upload in chunks using bounded local space.
.TP
.B \-\-spool\-max SIZE
Local space for chunks (default: 128MiB, min: 2MiB). Requires \-\-chunked.
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-archive
Keep the local archive after a successful upload.
.SS Passphrase options
.TP
.B \-\-passphrase\-file FILE
Read the archive passphrase from FILE ('\-': stdin). A trailing newline is ignored. Without this option, the passphrase is read from a hidden prompt.
.TP
.B \-\-catalog\-passphrase\-file FILE
Read the catalog passphrase from FILE ('\-': stdin). Without this option, GLESHA_CATALOG_PASSPHRASE or a hidden prompt is used.
.SS Performance options
.TP
.B \-\-memory\-max SIZE
Memory limit (default: half of available memory). SIZE takes a unit such as MiB or GiB and must be at least 48MiB. If available memory cannot be determined, 128MiB is used.
.TP
.B \-j, \-\-jobs, \-\-transfer\-workers N
Run up to N transfers at once (default: 4). The memory limit may lower the effective number.
.TP
.B \-\-hash\-workers N
Hash up to N files at once (default: 4).
.PP
The global options described in glesha(1) are also accepted.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
glesha run docs
glesha run docs \-\-incremental
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR glesha (1),
.BR glesha\-history (1),
.BR glesha\-restore (1),
.BR glesha\-retry (1)
